{"id": "SGU_Episode_307", "title": "SGU Episode 307", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 307 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 307", "date": "May 31 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 5, "day": 31, "rogues": ["Rebecca Watson", "Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Fuller", "quote": "\n 'It is astonishing what force, purity, and wisdom it requires for a human being to keep clear of falsehoods.' \n", "quotee": "\n Margaret Fuller \n", "quotee_title": "", "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-307", "episode_number": 307}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "June 4, 1783: The Montgolfier brothers publicly demonstrate their montgolfi\u00e8re (hot air balloon).", "title": "This Day in Skepticism", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "This Day in Skepticism"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 2, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 3, "text": "http://www.foxnews.com/scitech/2011/05/27/italian-scientist-charged-manslaughter-failing-predict-earthquake/", "title": "Predicting Earthquakes", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.foxnews.com/scitech/2011/05/27/italian-scientist-charged-manslaughter-failing-predict-earthquake/"], "title": "Predicting Earthquakes"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 4, "text": "http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/health-13577120", "title": "Mapping the Brain", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/health-13577120"], "title": "Mapping the Brain"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 5, "text": "http://www.wired.com/wiredscience/2011/05/ads-implant-false-memories/", "title": "Ads Implant False Memories", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.wired.com/wiredscience/2011/05/ads-implant-false-memories/"], "title": "Ads Implant False Memories"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 6, "text": "Answer to last week:", "title": "Who's That Noisy", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Who's That Noisy"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 7, "text": "http://skepchick.org/2011/05/autism-one-conference-skeptics-will-be-prosecuted-to-the-fullest-extent-of-the-law/ http://scienceblogs.com/insolence/2011/05/expelled_2011_edition.php", "title": "Interview with Jamie Bernstein", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://skepchick.org/2011/05/autism-one-conference-skeptics-will-be-prosecuted-to-the-fullest-extent-of-the-law/", "http://scienceblogs.com/insolence/2011/05/expelled_2011_edition.php"], "title": "Interview with Jamie Bernstein"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 8, "text": "Item #1: Scientists demonstrate that specially tinted glasses can reduce migraine headaches by reducing brain hyper-activation in response to certain visual patterns.\nItem #2: Biologists confirm a link between the retrovirus XMRV and chronic fatigue syndrome.\nItem #3: New research finds that biodegradable products may be worse for the environment than non-biodegradable alternatives.\n", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 9, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": [{"id": 10, "text": "'It is astonishing what force, purity, and wisdom it requires for a human being to keep clear of falsehoods.' - Margaret Fuller", "meta